From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram routes on asap7
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two things kept generate_ram from routing an asap7 block.

-tracks: generate_ram made its tracks from the technology LEF's
offsets, and asap7's M2 offset is negative (IFP-0039). -tracks names a
file of make_tracks commands to source instead, as asap7's flows do;
without it the tracks are made as before. A file that cannot be read
stops with RAM-0097.

Pins off the power straps: the pin placer did not know where
generate_ram's own straps run, and put pins on the tracks under them.
On asap7 the M4 straps start at the block's bottom edge, its first
track 12 nm above it, and detailed routing could not reach the pin
(DRT-0255). Each strap's span, with its layer's spacing, is now
excluded from the edges that layer's pins go on. The existing sky130
and Nangate45 blocks keep their pins where they were.

The asap7 tracks file joins //test:asap7_data.

Tested: the asap7 tests in src/ram/test, which route their blocks
through generate_ram in the commit that follows.

Commit 20 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
---
 src/ram/README.md   |  1 +
 src/ram/src/ram.cpp | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/ram/src/ram.tcl | 13 +++++++++++--
 test/BUILD          |  1 +
 4 files changed, 47 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ram/README.md b/src/ram/README.md
index e5a52fa91b..3a36bd2cab 100644
--- a/src/ram/README.md
+++ b/src/ram/README.md
@@ -110,6 +110,7 @@ generate_ram [-mask_size bits]
 | `-max_tap_dist` | The distance (in microns) that tapcells should be placed apart. Requires `-tapcell`. |
 | `-use_latch` | If set to `1`, uses a two-phase latch-based design instead of flip-flops for the storage elements. Functionally equivalent to flip-flop design with smaller storage cell area. Default: `0`. |
 | `-write_behavioral_verilog` | Write a behavioral Verilog model of the RAM array to the specified file. |
+| `-tracks` | `generate_ram` only. A Tcl file of `make_tracks` commands, sourced in place of `make_tracks` with the technology LEF's offsets, for a technology whose offsets do not fit the block (asap7's M2 offset is negative). Default: the LEF's tracks. |
 
 ## Example scripts
 
diff --git a/src/ram/src/ram.cpp b/src/ram/src/ram.cpp
index fcadc384d4..1c292a6a83 100644
--- a/src/ram/src/ram.cpp
+++ b/src/ram/src/ram.cpp
@@ -1885,8 +1885,40 @@ void RamGen::ramPinplacer(const char* ver_name, const char* hor_name)
   }
 
   auto pin_tech = block_->getDb()->getTech();
-  io_placer_->addHorLayer(pin_tech->findLayer(hor_name));
-  io_placer_->addVerLayer(pin_tech->findLayer(ver_name));
+  odb::dbTechLayer* hor_layer = pin_tech->findLayer(hor_name);
+  odb::dbTechLayer* ver_layer = pin_tech->findLayer(ver_name);
+  io_placer_->addHorLayer(hor_layer);
+  io_placer_->addVerLayer(ver_layer);
+
+  // no pin on a power strap of its own layer: where a strap reaches an
+  // edge, a pin on the tracks under it cannot be reached (asap7's M4
+  // straps start on the bottom edge, its first track 12 nm above it)
+  for (dbNet* net : block_->getNets()) {
+    if (!net->getSigType().isSupply()) {
+      continue;
+    }
+    for (odb::dbSWire* swire : net->getSWires()) {
+      for (odb::dbSBox* box : swire->getWires()) {
+        if (box->isVia()) {
+          continue;
+        }
+        const odb::Rect r = box->getBox();
+        if (box->getTechLayer() == hor_layer) {
+          const int s = hor_layer->getSpacing();
+          io_placer_->excludeInterval(
+              ppl::Edge::right, r.yMin() - s, r.yMax() + s);
+          io_placer_->excludeInterval(
+              ppl::Edge::left, r.yMin() - s, r.yMax() + s);
+        } else if (box->getTechLayer() == ver_layer) {
+          const int s = ver_layer->getSpacing();
+          io_placer_->excludeInterval(
+              ppl::Edge::top, r.xMin() - s, r.xMax() + s);
+          io_placer_->excludeInterval(
+              ppl::Edge::bottom, r.xMin() - s, r.xMax() + s);
+        }
+      }
+    }
+  }
   io_placer_->getParameters()->setCornerAvoidance(0);
   io_placer_->runHungarianMatching();
 }
diff --git a/src/ram/src/ram.tcl b/src/ram/src/ram.tcl
index ce5f5aa8cc..bd1f4e1948 100644
--- a/src/ram/src/ram.tcl
+++ b/src/ram/src/ram.tcl
@@ -337,6 +337,7 @@ sta::define_cmd_args "generate_ram" {[-mask_size bits]
                                      [-max_tap_dist value]
                                      [-use_latch value]
                                      [-write_behavioral_verilog filename]
+                                     [-tracks file]
                                      }
 
 # user arguments for generate ram arguments
@@ -351,10 +352,14 @@ proc generate_ram { args } {
            -banks -bank_columns -bank_order -rb_ports -register_read_address
            -write_style -write_priority
            -cells -name -decoder -bit_folds -service_columns
-           -bank_column_layout } flags {}
+           -bank_column_layout -tracks } flags {}
 
   sta::check_argc_eq0 "generate_ram" $args
 
+  if { [info exists keys(-tracks)] && ![file readable $keys(-tracks)] } {
+    utl::error RAM 97 "-tracks file $keys(-tracks) is not readable."
+  }
+
   # Check for valid design
   if { [ord::get_db_block] != "NULL" } {
     utl::error RAM 20 "A design is already loaded. Cannot generate RAM"
@@ -509,7 +514,11 @@ proc generate_ram { args } {
     $route_name $route_width \
     $ver_name $ver_width $ver_pitch $hor_name $hor_width $hor_pitch
 
-  make_tracks -x_offset 0 -y_offset 0
+  if { [info exists keys(-tracks)] } {
+    source $keys(-tracks)
+  } else {
+    make_tracks -x_offset 0 -y_offset 0
+  }
 
   ram::ram_pinplacer $ver_name $hor_name
 
